---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const title = "Privacy | Vecto";
const description =
  "Vecto's privacy policy: the app runs entirely on your device, has no network code, and collects, stores and transmits no personal data.";
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="icon" href={`${base}/favicon.ico`} sizes="any" />
    <link
      rel="alternate"
      type="text/plain"
      href={`${base}/llms.txt`}
      title="LLM Documentation"
    />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0a0a0a" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://danielmevit.github.io/vecto/privacy/" />
    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #0a0a0a;
        --text: #c9c9c9;
        --heading: #ffffff;
        --muted: #8c8c8c;
        --border: #232323;
        --accent-hi: #3fa4ee;
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        font-family: "Inter", -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
          Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        line-height: 1.7;
        margin: 0;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      }
      main { max-width: 720px; margin: 4rem auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
      a { color: var(--accent-hi); text-decoration: none; }
      a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
      .brand {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem;
        font-weight: 700; color: var(--heading); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;
      }
      .brand img { width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 6px; display: block; }
      h1 { color: var(--heading); font-size: 2.2rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 0.3rem; }
      .updated { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
      h2 { color: var(--heading); font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
      ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
      li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
      code {
        font-family: Consolas, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em;
        background: #151515; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 5px; padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
      }
      footer { text-align: center; margin-top: 5rem; padding: 3rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <a class="brand" href={`${base}/`} aria-label="Vecto home">
        <img src={`${base}/assets/vecto_logo.png`} alt="" width="28" height="28" /> Vecto
      </a>

      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="updated">The short version: there is nothing to disclose, because nothing is collected.</p>

      <h2>The app</h2>
      <p>
        Vecto runs entirely on your device. It contains <strong>no network code</strong> —
        it cannot upload, download, phone home, or check for updates. It works with the
        network cable unplugged.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Images you open, and the SVG/PNG files you export, stay on your computer.</li>
        <li>No account exists, no sign-in, no license activation.</li>
        <li>No analytics, telemetry, crash reporting, or advertising of any kind.</li>
        <li>
          The only thing Vecto writes besides your exports is its own settings file
          (window size, last-used tracing options): <code>%APPDATA%\Vecto\settings.json</code>,
          or <code>settings.json</code> beside the exe in the portable version. It contains
          no personal data and you can delete it at any time.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a static page hosted on GitHub Pages. It sets no cookies and runs no
        analytics. GitHub, as the host, keeps standard server logs under
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
        The download buttons query the GitHub API for the latest release version; that
        request goes to GitHub, not to us.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Vecto is open source — you can <a href="https://github.com/danielmevit/vecto">read the code</a>
        and verify all of the above. For anything else,
        <a href="https://github.com/danielmevit/vecto/issues">open an issue</a>.
      </p>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p><a href={`${base}/`}>Home</a> · <a href="https://github.com/danielmevit/vecto">GitHub</a></p>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
